WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
A swarm is a workspace: topologies, skills, runs — all of it data.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.400
Topologies are YAML files the runtime interprets. Nothing is generated.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.600
Every agent's model, skills and children — read back from the file.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.800
The same file, as a graph. GATED means a human must approve before it proceeds.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.000
A run paused for a person. It is checkpointed — nothing is held open.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.200
Every run, with status and cost.

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.400
Skills are the only way an agent gains a capability.

8
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.600
Archetypes are reusable agents — model, prompt, scopes.

9
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.800
What the workspace can reach, and whether each credential resolves right now.

10
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.000
Append-only. No agent has an update or delete path, ever.
